From 415bdc7b6213a83b64440024629614fee63edc60 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: TanJin <tanjin@local.bench>
Date: Sun, 11 Oct 2026 23:15:48 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 6/8] start-plan gate: official system camouflage + Aliyun
 captcha (zcode-api port)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Port of the two hard gateway gates for the free start-plan lane,
reverse-engineered by TriDefender/zcode-api against official bundles:

- vendors captcha solver stack (happy-dom in-process, token pool,
  config fetch from /api/v1/client/configs captcha node) into
  adapters/src/model/start-plan-gate/, Bun-only worker asset path
  replaced with in-process dispatch
- gate fetch wrapper: official 3-block system camouflage prepended
  (client TZCode/persona system preserved after, cache_control
  stripped per 4-breakpoint budget), currentDate context_prefix
  user turn prepended, captcha token headers attached, one
  challenge-retry (header or 400/3007)
- request-security-edition now wires the gate into the official
  protectTransport seam for *-start-plan providers only; coding-plan
  / off-peak / highspeed lanes untouched (signing V4 is coding-plan
  only and server-side fail-open — not needed)
- ZCODE_START_PLAN_GATE=0 request-level kill switch
- tests: gate unit suite (camouflage/idempotency/kill-switch/
  challenge-retry/passthrough), wire-contract test updated to
  disable the gate per its passthrough semantics; 12/12 green,
  adapters typecheck green, full build 19/19
